# PDF export (ship-time only)

HTML is the source of truth. `public/downloads/*.pdf` is a snapshot for the
catalog / preview download buttons.

## While designing

Do **not** run `export:sheet` or `export:pdf` after layout, copy, or style
tweaks. Do not commit a PDF just to keep it “in sync.”

## When the user says commit, push, or ship

If sheet or deck files changed since the last export, regenerate the matching
PDF and include it in that commit.

Sheet (`src/app/sheet/**` or `/sheet` route):

```bash
# Use the port `pnpm dev` is actually on (often 3001)
SHEET_URL=http://127.0.0.1:PORT/sheet/ pnpm export:sheet
```

Writes `public/downloads/curators.pdf`. Confirm it is **2 A4 pages** (print CSS
must zero `.sheet-pages` padding/gap or Playwright emits extra blank pages).

Decks (`decks/**`, `src/app/d/**`) — only if those files changed. These are
slow and large; skip unless the user is shipping a deck:

```bash
pnpm export:pdf:fund-admins   # or export:pdf:aon
```

If nothing visual changed (rule-only, copy in a comment, CI), skip export.
